libcamera: software_isp: luma and chroma noise reduction and sharpening

The GPU debayer ends at the gamma curve: a dim scene comes out grainy and a
bright one soft, where the reference phones smooth the flat areas and keep the
edges crisp. Omarchy Mobile's libcamera adds a second pass to the GPU debayer
that does both, and the CPU twin of that ISP (omacam's omacam-merge, isp.rs) has
been finishing our merged bursts with the same filter, so live frames and stills
can now come out of it alike.

The debayer renders into an intermediate texture of the output size, and
postfilter.frag smooths the luma with an edge-preserving (bilateral) 3x3 filter,
sharpens it with an unsharp mask cored by the noise level, and averages the
chroma over 16 taps spanning 9x9 pixels, guided by the luma and the chroma, for
the blotchy colour noise of high gains. Colour is BT.601 luma and the two colour
differences, and all of it works on the display-encoded picture the first pass
writes. A new Detail algorithm of the simple IPA reads the tuning file's
"- Detail:" section: "sharpen" (the unsharp mask's amount), "denoise" and
"chromaDenoise" (range sigmas, in fractions of full scale). With the gain g the
sensor's signal is multiplied by, the analogue gain it gets times the digital
gain that brings back the highlight headroom, denoise and chromaDenoise grow as
sqrt(g) up to 0.15 and 0.25 while sharpen falls as 1 / (1 + log2(g) / 3), and
the Sharpness control (0..4, 1 by default) scales the amount. A missing key is
0, and a tuning file without the section leaves the picture exactly as before:
the pass does not run and the intermediate texture is never allocated. The
output's byte order becomes a uniform rather than a define, so that the first
pass can write RGB for the second to read.

The stages and their strengths are Omarchy Mobile's (Copyright (C) 2026 Derek
Ross, LGPL-2.1-or-later), from its "software_isp: debayer_egl: Add a noise
reduction and sharpening pass", "ipa: simple: Add noise reduction and
sharpening" and "software_isp: debayer_egl: Smooth the chroma" patches, adapted
onto our shaders and pipeline. Where they differ, omacam's isp.rs decides: it
keeps no default strengths of its own, so neither does this.
---

